(FMT-18 — the value inside a slot must be a variable or expression, never
 a bare literal: a bare number in a slot is read as a VARIABLE NAME and
 the program is refused. Hand-verified that the specifier is irrelevant —
 the same slot with no specifier is rejected with the same diagnostic.
 The slot is deliberately not written out in this comment: the compiler
 anchors this diagnostic at the first TEXTUAL occurrence of the slot in
 the file, comments included, so spelling it here would move the caret
 off the offending code (Discrepancy 5).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox probe.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Unknown variable: 255
   (a compile error — vox refuses the program and emits no binary)
)
Print "{255:x}".
